====Male Scraps Design & Concepts====
During development, {{CI|Scraps|name=true}} was originally depicted as a male [[Toon]], though the only difference design-wise was her lack of eyelashes. While this version of Scraps is unused in the storyline and her in-game model, there are still some relics in the game that feature this male version of her, these being the old version of "{{CI|Astro|name=true}} in Stage Fright" [[Poster]], which was updated in [[Changelog|v0.10.1]], the "Welcome to [[Gardenview]]" Poster, and Scraps' Introduction Card having little/no space next to each occurrence of the word "she" since [[Qwel]] had to add the letter "S".<ref>https://discord.com/channels/969934252844138496/1251545388259741768/1266027125719302185</ref> 

Early in development, Scraps' ears were originally meant to be horns, but due to how they were designed, Qwel made them ears instead, which, combined with her tail, made Scraps look like a cat. Qwel just rolled with it, and this is what caused Scraps' cat-like actions and personality. <ref>https://discord.com/channels/969934252844138496/1251545388259741768/1323334100374781972</ref> Scraps was also not originally related to {{CI|Goob|name=true}}, but due to them both being crafts,<ref>https://discord.com/channels/969934252844138496/1251545388259741768/1305307327943016569</ref> Qwel made them siblings, since she thought it'd be a nice connection for them.<ref>https://discord.com/channels/969934252844138496/1251545388259741768/1305307423707500584</ref> However, this decision was later in development, and it was likely too late to change their designs to make them look more related. If this was not the case though, they probably would've just had more similar characteristics, but their [[Abilities]] and their [[Twisteds]] mechanics were similar to one another.
